    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d564">

                <pb facs="0553" n="463" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg463"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/3529</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Irkutsk</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d564-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Omsk</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-12-24"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">December 24, 1918</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received December 26, 12.22 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>253. Situation Omsk to-day’s date. Small Bolshevik uprising in village near Omsk
                    (?) was supported [<hi rendition="#italic">sic</hi>] by Czech and Cossack
                    troops. Attempt on Semenov’s life in Chita with hand grenade. <pb facs="0554"
                        n="464" xml:id="pg464"/> Semenov not seriously wounded. Czech National
                    Council in Ekaterinburg has been disarmed [dissolved?]. Situation Ufa front
                    somewhat improved. Slight Bolshevik unrest reported in Krasnoyarsk, otherwise
                    quiet Siberia.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Harris</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d564-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d564-f1-content">
                <p>Sent via the Legation in China.</p>
            </note>
